{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The pressure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/6370e3110be7e01afa16fd13d44c5115cfde2a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> of wind on a sail varies jointly as the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565ab5e3715db52b9176b04dd9991b71f4e93a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> of the sail and the square of the velocity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130d96c1df523aa2fcb2263aa935de9ad0237560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(V)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> of the wind. The pressure on a square foot is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pound when the velocity is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. The velocity of the wind when the pressure on a square yard is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pounds is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204d6a7cfcdddb11648cc0c97a96f968f1ad3730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 96\\text{ mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 32\\text{ mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 1\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ mph}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16\\text{ mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"600\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> varies jointly as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16855265ece631eba44effb646b72798d459683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V^2$\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, that means that there is a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/338cbf2809125223a361c17213cc74dfcd0615d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=kAV^2$\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />. You are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d99d5ffc20f99bef98a1861496b6758fa9541d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18428217dcd07944b2adbebcafd0978587a770a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef6f8d2786d5c5bc670144947b277821e990628a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. That means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e9e4a7fc3cc796c99b2fd09735692a5713bdb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=k(1)(16^2) \\rightarrow k=\\frac{1}{256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"198\" height=\"37\" />. Then, substituting into the original equation with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a0d59a0ffcef2865a3490cf59d7dffc8f95218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=36$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/826698ae674d37645f36277970439261b6e28d23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=9$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> (because a square yard is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times a square foot), you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4ceb0aa4df61d250c3e257ed88497c03b99cb3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=\\frac{1}{256}(V^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"99\" height=\"37\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de65c001d428137c809284ccd786c5bdd11d7fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V^2=1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065d2cf9376db017dc1cd67aef38959ff57f142c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=32$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />. Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1951\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1951 AHSME Proble